`LeaceEraser` erases only the directions in which subjects differ most: those whose subject eta^2, the share of their variance between subjects, is at least `eta2` (default 0.5), at most `max_rank` of them (no limit by default). Erasing every direction in which subject means differ, as it did, leaves nothing once there are more subjects than features. `fit` takes the `condition` of each row (e.g. eyes open or closed), so a subject with more windows of one condition does not count that as identity and the difference between conditions is kept. The fitted eraser has `rank_`, `eta2_` and `components_`. It always estimates the total covariance with Ledoit-Wolf and refuses to erase 95% of the feature directions or more; `shrinkage`, `degenerate_frac` and `degenerate_` are removed.
